# cockpit/.env -- copy this file to .env and fill it in. .env is git-ignored;
# this example is tracked and holds NO values.
#
# Four roles call a model, and every one is set the same way, by its own lines --
# an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, its key, a model, and for the two agents (I, C)
# the harness that runs them. Nothing falls back to another role: two roles on
# the same model repeat the same values.
#
# The harness of I and C is the Codex CLI (https://github.com/openai/codex), and
# it is REQUIRED for them: `npm install -g @openai/codex`, then `codex` must be on
# PATH. The only value so far: codex-cli. Your own ~/.codex/config.toml does not
# apply to them (codex runs with --ignore-user-config): these lines are all of it.
#
#   planner   P   intent -> SPEC.md (Draft, Revise)       a chat call
#   reviewer  H'  reviews drafts, briefs HARD changes,    a chat call
#                 checks a run's goal
#   intent    I   the agent that authors a run            an agent (Codex CLI)
#   coder     C   implements a node from its SPEC.md      an agent (Codex CLI)
#
# REASONING_EFFORT is optional, for every role: how hard the model thinks (e.g.
# low | medium | high -- what the provider accepts), passed as written: to the
# chat call for P and H', to the Codex CLI for I and C. Empty: the provider's
# default.
#
# Set only the roles you use: the gate, drift, test evidence and specs written by
# hand need none. A value already in the environment wins, so one command can
# override a role:  SGE_CODER_MODEL=... uv run python cli.py run ROOT
# Check what is set -- never the key:  uv run python role_agent.py --describe
#
# Using DeepSeek for every role? .env.deepseek.example is a complete configuration
# for it: copy that one instead, and put your key in place of each `sk-...`.

# P -- the planner
SGE_PLANNER_BASE_URL=
SGE_PLANNER_API_KEY=
SGE_PLANNER_MODEL=
SGE_PLANNER_REASONING_EFFORT=

# H' -- the reviewer. The same values as P work, but then H' reviews what its own
# model wrote, and the cockpit says so: another model makes the review independent.
SGE_REVIEWER_BASE_URL=
SGE_REVIEWER_API_KEY=
SGE_REVIEWER_MODEL=
SGE_REVIEWER_REASONING_EFFORT=

# I -- the intent author of a run
SGE_INTENT_BASE_URL=
SGE_INTENT_API_KEY=
SGE_INTENT_MODEL=
SGE_INTENT_REASONING_EFFORT=
SGE_INTENT_HARNESS=codex-cli

# C -- the coder: `cli.py code`, the cockpit's Codex button, and every run
SGE_CODER_BASE_URL=
SGE_CODER_API_KEY=
SGE_CODER_MODEL=
SGE_CODER_REASONING_EFFORT=
SGE_CODER_HARNESS=codex-cli
